IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-73, TARGETED: the Sick Pay Law, 5736-1976. Draft, target compiler main. No domain expert has read this against the source.
-- THIS ROW DOES NOT ENCODE THE LAW. It records two references of the Law (items I1 and I2) as typed values, and tests them.
-- SEAT: for I1, the employer to whom the rule of section 4A on dismissal during the entitlement to sick pay applies; for I2, the employee whose sick pay section 11 excludes for a period covered by a payment under another enactment.
-- A row of references asks that individual no question: there is no input to ask for, and no @export.
-- NOUNS: an issue of a gazette, a printed instruction, a printed provision, an enactment named in a citation and the status the deposited instruments give it, the two kinds of citation (of enactments; of a chapter), and the questions asked of them.
-- No reference is stated here; they are in sk73-cross-references.l4.
--
-- Every item is recorded with two limbs, as in the other targeted rows:
--   limb (a): the target is repealed, missing or says something else, read from an official instrument;
--   limb (b): the citing words still read so in the latest official instrument.
-- Section numbers are written with Latin letters for the Hebrew ones the Law uses (4A is 4 alef; 342C is 342 gimel; 342F is 342 vav; 342G is 342 zayin).
-- THE NAMES OF THE STATUSES AND OF THE BASES BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: a status is what the deposited instruments print, and nothing else.
-- Hebrew in a string literal is a token copied from a quotation line (`ext:` or `src:`) of sk73-cross-references.l4; tools/hebcheck.py checks it.

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `A series of print` IS ONE OF
    `Sefer HaChukim`
    `Dinei Medinat Israel new-version print, not one of the three gazette series`

DECLARE `How a value was obtained` IS ONE OF
    `printed on a deposited page`
    `arithmetic on words printed on a deposited page`
    `computed from the issue date, not printed`
    `CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `not given by any page read`

DECLARE `How a limb was read` IS ONE OF
    `official page images of the instruments named`
    `official page images, with the other instruments of the consolidation's tag table read and later instruments not excluded (see NOTES.md)`

DECLARE `An issue` HAS
    `its name` IS A STRING
    `its series` IS A `A series of print`
    `the date its footer prints` IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `What an instruction does` IS ONE OF
    `inserts a section after another`
    `adds a chapter after a section`
    `replaces a string in a section`
    `repeals an enactment but for one section`
    `repeals sections of an enactment`
    `repeals chapters of an enactment`
    `replaces a word wherever it occurs in the enactments of a schedule`

DECLARE `A printed instruction` HAS
    `the label` IS A STRING
    `the issue` IS A `An issue`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `what it does` IS A `What an instruction does`
    `what it is aimed at` IS A STRING
    `how it was obtained` IS A `How a value was obtained`

DECLARE `A printed provision` HAS
    `the label` IS A STRING
    `the issue` IS A `An issue`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `its margin note` IS A STRING
    `the printed tokens` IS A LIST OF STRING

DECLARE `A word replacement` HAS
    `the instruction` IS A `A printed instruction`
    `the number of the pair` IS A NUMBER
    `the word replaced` IS A STRING
    `the word put in its place` IS A STRING

DECLARE `A string replacement` HAS
    `the instruction` IS A `A printed instruction`
    `the string replaced` IS A STRING
    `the replacement string` IS A STRING

DECLARE `A schedule entry` HAS
    `the label` IS A STRING
    `the issue` IS A `An issue`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `the item number` IS A NUMBER
    `the bracket printed beside the item` IS A STRING
    `an exception is printed with the item` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `A search of the pairs of a word replacement` HAS
    `the issue` IS A `An issue`
    `the number of pairs` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of pairs that contain the name of either enactment` IS A NUMBER
    `how it was obtained` IS A STRING

DECLARE `A tag-table row` HAS
    `the issue` IS A `An issue`
    `the printed page` IS A NUMBER
    `carries an instruction on section 4A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `carries an instruction on section 11` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the page is deposited` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `A commencement` HAS
    `the label` IS A STRING
    `the rule as printed, in English` IS A STRING
    `the day it names` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `how the day was obtained` IS A `How a value was obtained`

DECLARE `A status as the deposited instruments give it` IS ONE OF
    `repealed but for one section`
    `repealed in part`
    `not repealed by any instrument deposited here`

DECLARE `An enactment named in a citation` HAS
    `its name in English, a working translation` IS A STRING
    `the name as the citing words print it` IS A STRING
    `its status` IS A `A status as the deposited instruments give it`
    `the instructions that give the status` IS A LIST OF `A printed instruction`

DECLARE `A citation of enactments` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the paragraph that carries the citing words` IS A `A printed provision`
    `the enactments the citing words name` IS A LIST OF `An enactment named in a citation`
    `the later instructions that touch the citing words` IS A LIST OF `A printed instruction`
    `a later instruction changes a name the citing words print` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`

DECLARE `A citation of a chapter` HAS
    `the item` IS A STRING
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the instruction that cites the chapter` IS A `A printed instruction`
    `the number the citing words write for the chapter` IS A STRING
    `the instruction that added the chapter` IS A `A printed instruction`
    `the number the instruction that added the chapter gives it` IS A STRING
    `the title the instruction that added the chapter gives it` IS A STRING
    `the number in the heading of the later print` IS A STRING
    `the title in the heading of the later print` IS A STRING
    `the bracket in the margin beside the heading of the later print` IS A STRING
    `the table row of the later print, 1968 entry` IS A STRING
    `the table row of the later print, 1995 entry` IS A STRING
    `the 1995 column of the table holds an entry equal to the number the citing words write` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (a) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`
    `limb (b) holds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `limb (b) was read` IS A `How a limb was read`

-- ===== The questions. Each takes a value from sk73-cross-references.l4. =====

GIVEN e IS A `An enactment named in a citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the enactment is repealed in whole or in part` MEANS (e's `its status` EQUALS `repealed but for one section`) OR (e's `its status` EQUALS `repealed in part`)

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of enactments`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no enactment the citing words name is repealed in whole or in part` MEANS NOT (any `the enactment is repealed in whole or in part` (c's `the enactments the citing words name`))

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of enactments`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`some enactment the citing words name is repealed in whole or in part` MEANS any `the enactment is repealed in whole or in part` (c's `the enactments the citing words name`)

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of enactments`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold for the enactments` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`

GIVEN
    p IS A `A printed provision`
    t IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision prints the token` MEANS elem t (p's `the printed tokens`)

GIVEN
    p IS A `A printed provision`
    e IS A `An enactment named in a citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision prints the name of the enactment` MEANS elem (e's `the name as the citing words print it`) (p's `the printed tokens`)

GIVEN
    w IS A `A word replacement`
    p IS A `A printed provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the replaced word is a token of the provision` MEANS elem (w's `the word replaced`) (p's `the printed tokens`)

GIVEN
    w IS A `A word replacement`
    e IS A `An enactment named in a citation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the replaced word is the name of the enactment` MEANS w's `the word replaced` EQUALS e's `the name as the citing words print it`

GIVEN
    s IS A `A string replacement`
    p IS A `A printed provision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the string replaced is a token of the provision` MEANS elem (s's `the string replaced`) (p's `the printed tokens`)

GIVEN
    a IS A `An issue`
    b IS A `An issue`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two issues are different` MEANS NOT (a's `its name` EQUALS b's `its name`)

GIVEN
    i IS A `A printed instruction`
    j IS A `A printed instruction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two instructions are in one issue` MEANS i's `the issue`'s `its name` EQUALS j's `the issue`'s `its name`

GIVEN r IS A `A tag-table row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the row carries an instruction on section 11` MEANS r's `carries an instruction on section 11`

GIVEN r IS A `A tag-table row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the row carries an instruction on section 4A` MEANS r's `carries an instruction on section 4A`

GIVEN r IS A `A tag-table row`
GIVETH A STRING
`the name of the issue of the row` MEANS r's `the issue`'s `its name`

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of a chapter`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the number the 1995 print's table gives the cited chapter` MEANS
    IF c's `the table row of the later print, 1968 entry` EQUALS c's `the number the citing words write for the chapter`
    THEN JUST (c's `the table row of the later print, 1995 entry`)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of a chapter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the chapter number written in the citing words is the number the 1995 print gives that chapter` MEANS JUST (c's `the number the citing words write for the chapter`) EQUALS `the number the 1995 print's table gives the cited chapter` c

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of a chapter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instruction that added the chapter gives it the number the citing words write` MEANS c's `the number the instruction that added the chapter gives it` EQUALS c's `the number the citing words write for the chapter`

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of a chapter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two titles are the same words` MEANS c's `the title the instruction that added the chapter gives it` EQUALS c's `the title in the heading of the later print`

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of a chapter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the bracket and the table row agree on the number the citing words write` MEANS (c's `the bracket in the margin beside the heading of the later print` EQUALS c's `the number the citing words write for the chapter`) AND (c's `the table row of the later print, 1968 entry` EQUALS c's `the number the citing words write for the chapter`)

GIVEN c IS A `A citation of a chapter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`both limbs hold for the chapter` MEANS c's `limb (a) holds` AND c's `limb (b) holds`

-- A day a printed instruction takes effect is not given by the pages this row reads unless the row types it as a `A commencement`; for an instruction with none, the answer is NOTHING.
GIVEN i IS A `A printed instruction`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day the instruction takes effect` MEANS NOTHING
